  "executive_briefing": "As of June 2026, the crypto-macro landscape has solidified around the 'Bitcoin-as-a-Platform' narrative, catalyzed by the Senate Banking Committee's advancement of the Digital Asset Market Clarity Act. This legislative progress, moving toward a floor vote, is shifting institutional capital from Ethereum to Bitcoin-native smart contract infrastructures. While institutional adoption of Bitcoin\u2014bolstered by novel ETF structures like bond-linked instruments\u2014continues to reach new heights, Ethereum is experiencing significant sentiment fatigue. The narrative has shifted from Ethereum's general-purpose utility to concerns over its long-term financial sustainability, further exacerbated by the rise of native, non-custodial cross-chain liquidity solutions that eliminate the need for centralized 'wrapped' tokens, effectively bridging Bitcoin's new programmable layer into broader liquidity pools.",
